1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
This robot has no pinky.

2
00:00:02,080 --> 00:00:03,133
On purpose.

3
00:00:03,280 --> 00:00:05,200
Boston Dynamics says its engineers

4
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:06,567
taped their ring and pinky

5
00:00:06,560 --> 00:00:08,200
fingers together for a day.

6
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:09,000
The verdict?

7
00:00:09,280 --> 00:00:10,233
Leave it out.

8
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:12,567
Atlas’s new hand has four digits,

9
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:13,200
but thirteen

10
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:14,433
degrees of freedom.

11
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:16,267
Independent ways to move.

12
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:18,120
The company says it can pinch,

13
00:00:18,120 --> 00:00:18,933
turn objects,

14
00:00:18,920 --> 00:00:20,300
and press tool triggers.

15
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:21,600
A fifth digit would mean

16
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:23,133
three more actuators.

17
00:00:23,280 --> 00:00:24,233
More cost.

18
00:00:24,240 --> 00:00:25,200
More bulk.

19
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:26,200
More things to break.

20
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:28,333
So the goal is a useful,

21
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:29,633
reliable hand.

22
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:31,133
Looking human is optional.

23
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:32,933
Apparently, even robots

24
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:33,800
have a budget.
